# Generated files. Every one of these is a pure function of sources tracked
# elsewhere in the tree, so a hand-merge of one is always either busywork or a
# mistake. `merge=tack-generated` resolves them to our side without a conflict;
# `.githooks/post-merge` then regenerates them from the merged sources, and
# `.githooks/pre-push` refuses to send a stale one.
#
# The driver has to be registered locally to take effect — `scripts/setup-git.sh`
# does that. Without it git falls back to its normal text merge, which is the
# behaviour these files had before, so a clone that skipped setup is degraded,
# never broken.
Cargo.lock                            merge=tack-generated linguist-generated=true
frontend/package-lock.json            merge=tack-generated linguist-generated=true
docs/openapi.json                     merge=tack-generated linguist-generated=true
frontend/src/shared/api/schema.gen.ts merge=tack-generated linguist-generated=true

# Committed because `generate_context!` reads them while tack-desktop compiles.
crates/tack-desktop/icons/*.png  binary
crates/tack-desktop/icons/*.ico  binary
crates/tack-desktop/icons/*.icns binary
